# Azure Cloud-Native .NET Microservices

An engineering project focused on deploying, securing, and operating a .NET microservices application on Microsoft Azure.

Using Microsoft's [eShop](https://github.com/ibraheemcisse/eShop) as the application foundation, this project explores the practical engineering challenges of running distributed applications in the cloud.

## Technology Stack

- **Cloud:** Microsoft Azure
- **Application:** .NET / ASP.NET Core
- **Containers:** Docker
- **Orchestration:** Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)
- **Infrastructure as Code:** Terraform
- **CI/CD:** GitHub Actions
- **Observability:** OpenTelemetry

## Engineering Focus

- Infrastructure provisioning and automation
- Kubernetes deployment and operations
- Microservice communication and networking
- Resilience and failure handling
- Identity, security, and secrets management
- Distributed tracing, metrics, and logging
- Continuous integration and deployment
- Troubleshooting and operational reliability

## Project Status

<text id="project-status">In progress — initial setup and architecture planning.</text>

This repository will document the implementation, architectural decisions, experiments, and operational lessons learned throughout the project.
